import ../../../ui/scene_rotations.dl

to check oriented point {vector:actual} equals {vector:expected}:
    require condition ((the length of (actual - expected)) < 0.00001) reporting "A scene quaternion orientation changed."

set origin to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
set one to a new vector with x 1.0, y 1.0 and z 1.0
set up to a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
for each direction in [up, (a new vector with x 0.0, y -1.0 and z 0.0), (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0), (a new vector with x 2.0, y 4.0 and z 3.0)]:
    set rotation to the UI scene rotation from direction (up * 2.0) to direction direction
    check oriented point (up rotated by rotation) equals (direction normalized)
    set matrix to a UI scene matrix at origin oriented rotation scaled one
    set transform to a UI scene transform from matrix
    check oriented point (the UI scene direction of up through transform) equals (direction normalized)
set rotation to the UI scene rotation from direction up to direction (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0)
set matrix to a UI scene matrix at (a new vector with x 2.0, y 3.0 and z 4.0) oriented rotation scaled (a new vector with x 2.0, y 3.0 and z 4.0)
set transform to a UI scene transform from matrix
check oriented point (the UI scene position of up through transform) equals (a new vector with x 2.0, y 3.0 and z 7.0)
set normal to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0
check oriented point (the UI scene normal of normal through transform) equals (a new vector with x 0.0, y -1.0 and z 0.0)
set x to a new vector with x 1, y 0 and z 0
set rotation to the UI scene rotation from direction x to direction (a new vector with x -2, y 0 and z 0)
check oriented point ((a new vector with x 1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) rotated by rotation) equals (a new vector with x -1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0)
print line "Scene quaternion orientations align finite directions, preserve opposite axes and compose portable scaled transforms."
